- Use AI mode to generate storage operations: If you don't know what to modify, use ai mode to generate storage operations sequence based on the current context. Agent will create list of operations that will be executed in order. You can use any data in prompt to provide more context for agent.
{
  "mode": "ai",
  "aiPrompt": "Some prompt that will be used to modify storage as a result of execution"
}
- Chain AI Prompts for Complex Updates: Execute multiple AI prompts sequentially, where each prompt builds on the results of the previous one. Perfect for multi-step storage updates.
{
  "mode": "ai",
  "aiPrompts": [
    "Analyze the last message and extract key facts about the user",
    "Based on extracted facts, update user profile and preferences",
    "Generate personalized recommendations based on updated profile"
  ],
  "forceChanges": true
}
- Append to Array: Append data to an array in storage
{
  "operations": [
    {
      "op": "append",
      "path": "chatHistory",
      "sourcePath": "newMessage"
    }
  ]
}
- Increment with Value: Add a specific amount to a number in storage
{
  "operations": [
    {
      "op": "increment",
      "path": "player.score",
      "value": 10
    }
  ]
}
- Decrement with Template: Subtract damage from HP using template expression
{
  "operations": [
    {
      "op": "decrement",
      "path": "enemy.currentHP",
      "value": "{{ damage }}"
    }
  ]
}
- Increment from Context: Add value from context path to storage
{
  "operations": [
    {
      "op": "increment",
      "path": "player.experience",
      "sourcePath": "/earnedXP"
    }
  ]
}
- Sort Array: Sort array in-place by field
{
  "operations": [
    {
      "op": "sort",
      "path": "guilds",
      "field": "rating",
      "order": "desc"
    }
  ]
}
- Update by Filter: Update array items matching filter criteria
{
  "operations": [
    {
      "op": "update_by_filter",
      "path": "guilds",
      "filter": {
        "id": "playerGuild"
      },
      "value": {
        "rating": 900
      }
    }
  ]
}
- Remove by Index: Remove array item by index (supports template expressions)
{
  "operations": [
    {
      "op": "remove",
      "path": "deck",
      "value": "{{ cardIndex }}"
    }
  ]
}
- Remove by Filter: Remove array items matching filter (supports template expressions in filter)
{
  "operations": [
    {
      "op": "remove",
      "path": "deck",
      "filter": {
        "name": "{{ drawnCard.name }}"
      }
    }
  ]
}

**Best practices:**
- For operations with storage, prefer use mode:"ai" with aiPrompt; forceChanges optional
- For simple and predicted operations with storage, use storage without ai mode
- If you need to modify storage somehow, use storage with ai mode instead of agent node + storage node
- Storage fields access: {{ storage.fieldName }} or {{ fieldName }}
- Use forceChanges: true to require at least one operation in ai mode
- AI prompts: be specific about when NOT to update (avoid unnecessary operations)
- Use formatData for pretty-printing existing storage in AI prompts
- Include clear business rules for calculations in AI prompts
- Structure data with metadata fields for better filtering and correlation
- Do not put current storage in aiPrompt, it will be provided automatically
- Storage schema if available also will be provided automatically in context
- Try to do not use timestamps (and time at all) in storage
- Sort arrays: op:"sort", path:"items", field:"rating", order:"desc" (asc/desc)
- Update by filter: op:"update_by_filter", path:"items", filter:{id:"x"}, value:{field:newVal}
- Remove by index: op:"remove", path:"deck", value:"{{ cardIndex }}" or value:0
- Remove by filter: op:"remove", path:"deck", filter:{name:"{{ drawnCard.name }}"}
- Bracket notation supported: path:"items[0].name" same as "items.0.name"

