## ui

**Description:** Generates UI components from data arrays with safe JSON templating

**Schema:**
 {
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "source": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "JSONPath to array data (e.g., \"storage.suggestions\")"
    },
    "filter": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Expression to filter items (e.g., \"Date.now() - new Date(storage.timestamp).getTime() < 300000\")"
    },
    "templates": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "id": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Template for component ID, can use {{item}} and {{index}}"
          },
          "type": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "UI component type"
          },
          "placement": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Where to place the component"
          },
          "config": {
            "type": "object",
            "additionalProperties": {},
            "description": "Component configuration object"
          },
          "ttl": {
            "type": "number",
            "description": "Time to live in seconds"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "type",
          "placement",
          "config"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      },
      "description": "Array of templates for generating multiple UI components"
    },
    "outputAs": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Variable name to store result array"
    },
    "returnValue": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Value to return if this is the last node"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "outputAs"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "description": "UI node parameters for generating interface components",
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#"
}

**Examples:**
- Suggestion Buttons: Generate buttons from suggestions array
{
  "source": "storage.suggestions",
  "filter": "Date.now() - new Date(storage.timestamp).getTime() < 300000",
  "templates": [
    {
      "type": "button",
      "placement": "above_input",
      "config": {
        "label": "{{item}}",
        "variant": "outline",
        "action": {
          "type": "send_message",
          "payload": "{{item}}"
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "outputAs": "uiComponents",
  "returnValue": "uiComponents"
}
- XP Progress Bar: Generate progress bar for XP display
{
  "templates": [
    {
      "type": "progress",
      "placement": "sidebar",
      "config": {
        "label": "Experience Points",
        "value": "{{user.xp}}",
        "max": "{{user.nextLevelXp}}",
        "format": "custom",
        "customFormat": "{{value}}/{{max}} XP",
        "color": "#10b981",
        "showValue": true,
        "animated": true,
        "style": {
          "height": "md",
          "variant": "gradient"
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "outputAs": "progressComponent",
  "returnValue": "progressComponent"
}
- Conditional Disabled Button: Button disabled based on storage state
{
  "templates": [
    {
      "type": "button",
      "placement": "above_input",
      "config": {
        "label": "Submit",
        "variant": "primary",
        "disabled": "{{storage.isLocked || storage.submitted}}",
        "action": {
          "type": "send_message",
          "payload": "Submit form"
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "outputAs": "uiComponents",
  "returnValue": "uiComponents"
}

**Best practices:**
- UI nodes should be only connected with UI entrypoints, not after storage node and not in the middle/end of workflow started from entrypoints different from UI entrypoint
- For ui, use templates[], include per-template placement, set outputAs (and returnValue if needed)
- If ANY node has type "ui", you MUST set entryPoints.UI_REQUEST to that ui node id
- UI template config uses {{...}} with item/index available (e.g., {{item}}, {{index}}, {{storage.field}})
- In chat messages you cant inject images using markdown, use imageGeneration node instead
- Use above_input for short-lived suggestions; set ttl (e.g., 120–300s) to auto-expire
- Use sidebar for status/progress; avoid frequent re-renders to reduce churn
- Prefer stable IDs (e.g., id: "btn-{{item.id}}") to help the client deduplicate
- Dynamic colors with conditionals: "{{value > 50 ? '#green' : value > 20 ? '#yellow' : '#red'}}"
- Placement should be set once in template, not duplicated
- Never print whole body from storage into UI content component. You need to format it. This is bad idea: "content": "{{storage.shelfDisplay}}" Use functions to iterate over array of objects and format them
- Use disabled property for buttons/checkboxes/select options: disabled: "{{storage.isLocked}}" or disabled: true
- IMPORTANT: UI components are generated once when UI_REQUEST entrypoint is called. To update disabled state after storage changes, use refresh node after storage updates, or frontend must listen to ui_components_updated WebSocket event and re-fetch UI components

