## workflow

**Description:** Execute another workflow as a sub-workflow with shared context

**Schema:**
 {
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "workflowId": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "ID of the workflow to execute"
    },
    "entrypoint": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Entrypoint OR node-id to start from"
    },
    "payload": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": {},
      "description": "Custom data passed to sub-workflow triggerPayload"
    },
    "returnPath": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Path to extract result from finalContext (default: $lastOutput)"
    },
    "outputAs": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Variable name to store the result"
    },
    "isolateStorage": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "description": "If true, sub-workflow storage changes are NOT merged back to parent workflow"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "workflowId"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#"
}

**Examples:**
- Call sub-workflow: Execute another workflow and continue
{
  "workflowId": "content-filter-v1"
}
- Call with specific entrypoint: Execute workflow from specific entrypoint
{
  "workflowId": "game-logic-v2",
  "entrypoint": "CHAT_MESSAGE",
  "outputAs": "damageResult"
}
- Pass custom payload: Pass data to sub-workflow via payload
{
  "workflowId": "validator",
  "payload": {
    "input": "{{ chat.lastMessage.content }}",
    "rules": [
      "spam",
      "toxic"
    ]
  },
  "outputAs": "validationResult"
}
- Custom return path: Extract specific value from sub-workflow result
{
  "workflowId": "damage-calculator",
  "entrypoint": "CALCULATE",
  "payload": {
    "attacker": "{{ storage.player }}",
    "target": "{{ storage.enemy }}"
  },
  "returnPath": "storage.battleResult",
  "outputAs": "damageDealt"
}
- Isolated storage for statistics: Track statistics in separate workflow without affecting parent storage
{
  "workflowId": "statistics-tracker",
  "isolateStorage": true,
  "payload": {
    "score": "{{ storage.currentRun.score }}",
    "duration": "{{ storage.currentRun.duration }}"
  }
}

**Best practices:**
- Sub-workflows share full context including storage, chat data, and outputs
- Changes in sub-workflow affect parent workflow context BY DEFAULT
- Use isolateStorage: true to prevent sub-workflow storage from merging back to parent
- Isolated storage is useful for statistics tracking in separate workflows
- Use entrypoint to start from specific points in the sub-workflow
- Pass custom data via payload parameter (object) - available in sub-workflow as triggerPayload
- Use returnPath to extract specific values from sub-workflow result (default: $lastOutput)
- Sub-workflow result saved to outputAs variable in parent context
- Circular dependencies are detected and prevented
- Maximum depth limit prevents infinite recursion (10 levels)

