## Available entrypoints to use in workflow:


## CHAT_MESSAGE
**Description:** After character answer to user's message
**Best practices:**
Use this entrypoint to run some processing after user+character messages. It will be slow, because it will wait for character to finish answering.

## BEFORE_USER_MESSAGE
**Description:** Before saving user's message; pass text as payload
**Best practices:**
Runs before user message is processed/saved; use triggerPayload.text for raw input
Can be used to block sending to LLM via hard_end node

## BEFORE_CHAT_MESSAGE
**Description:** After user send message, even before character answer
**Best practices:**
Use this entrypoint to run some processing when user send message, even before character start answering
In messages history you cannot see character answer, because it is not yet generated

## CONTEXT_REQUEST
**Description:** To enrich user chat context with some additional data
**Best practices:**
This entrypoint is used to provide context to chat itself. It will be injected into and used by another LLM to generate response within context of chat.
Useful when we need to enrich user chat context with some additional data from storage like current status of some data, etc.
Under the hood, it uses $lastOutput to get final context text. So final context will be output of last node of this pathway/chain.

## UI_REQUEST
**Description:** To generate UI components and return it back to HTTP request to draw chat UI
**Best practices:**
Only way to start this pathway - on HTTP request when user loading chat or it will be auto updated after storage changes
This pathway should be finished with ui node. But before that it if needed can be executed some logical nodes to follow right path to final ui node that will render right UI components

## HTTP_TRIGGER
**Description:** Manual workflow trigger via HTTP endpoint (e.g., from UI buttons)
**Best practices:**
Triggered manually via POST endpoint from UI
Can receive custom payload data in request body that becomes available in workflow context
Perfect for button actions like "trigger_workflow" from UI components
Use to implement manual actions: reset game, generate content, perform calculations, etc. with custom payload
Can modify storage and send messages to chat as result of trigger

## CRON
**Description:** Time-based automation; runs on cron schedule defined in workflow settings
**Best practices:**
Configure cron expressions in settings.cronSchedules to run logic on a timer
Ideal for daily reminders, upkeep tasks, or scheduled storage maintenance
Entry point payload comes from cron schedule config (payload field)

